Many of our immigrant and Catholic base are disgusted at our compromise with Anderson's government. Even some in the leadership question whether is was right to achieve this legislation at the cost of aligning ourselves with the Premier. 

@leave_anderson
unavailable-subtitle: We promised the Progressives we'd support Anderson
choose-if: support_cooperative_coalition == 0

Anderson is disappointed. Perhaps he had thought that our merger would incline us to ally with him. Nonetheless, his government is a set of dominos awaiting that first tap. 

The Cooperative Coalition is no more and the CPS will soon face the cumulative anger of the Saskatchewan people at the polls. 